+# PR Review — MOB-25109-offline-content-card-availability
+
+## Summary
+This PR adds offline persistence for Content Cards: boot-time disk hydration, an `isNetworkAvailable()` gate to skip Edge when offline, a `usePersistedContentCards` flag on the get APIs, a `nonRecoverableErrorEventIds` shield to preserve disk on non-recoverable Edge errors, and a `CardOrigin` side-table for provenance tagging. The disk-read paths (boot hydration and `usePersistedContentCards`) are architecturally sound. However, the feature is broken for any app that has not explicitly configured the new remote config key — the default inverts the documented contract and silently clears the disk cache on every network response. Two CI tests will also fail as written. The network gate ships as a hardcoded stub and the in-memory CC propositions state is written but never read.
+
+**Verdict:** REQUEST CHANGES
+
+| Severity | Count |
+|----------|-------|
+| CRITICAL | 2 |
+| HIGH | 14 |
+| MEDIUM | 12 |
+| LOW | 5 |
+
